   "spoken": "For the theory record, the most ambitious white try is to snatch the pawn immediately. The tempting check to win it back only makes two queen moves, after which the opponent has nasty ideas — a capture on the back rank, then a check that costs castling rights, and the central pawn falls for a healthy extra pawn. Winning the pawn back has to be done more craftily than the obvious way.",
